------LAUNCH--------------------------------------

- ros2 launch urdf_tutorial display.launch.py model:=urdfFileDirectory
	(A simple way to run urdf files)

- ros2 launch folderName display.launch.py
	(this is for when you have everything set up)
	(check either ros2_ws/src/simple_robot_description)
	(or ros2_ws/src/car_homework_description for how it's done)
	
- ros2 launch gazebo_ros gazebo.launch.py (launches gazebo)
	(after doing this run the urdf/xacro files)
	(and use the run gazebo_ros command to load the file)
	
	(if you are launching a gazebo file and it keeps giving you this error)
	(:type = gazebo::rendering::Camera*]: Assertion `px != 0' failed.)
	(try sourcing gazebo ". /usr/share/gazebo/setup.sh")
	(the dot means source you can type "source /usr/share/gazebo/setup.sh")



------RUN-----------------------------------------

- ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames -o NewPdfFileName
	(this creates a graph for the urdf file that is running)
	
- ros2 run robot_state_publisher robot_state_publisher --ros-args -p robot_description:="$(xacro directory/fileName.urdf/xacro)"
	(this is the proper way to run urdf/xacro files)
	(run this command inside the folder that contains the urdf/xacro file)
	
- ros2 run rviz2 rviz2
	(this runs the sandbox app thing)
	(change the "Fixed Frame" to what you want it to be ex. base_link)
	(and add "RobotModel" and "TF" using the add button on the lower left side)
	
- ros2 run joint_state_publisher_gui joint_state_publisher_gui
	(this runs the joint state publisher)
	(it's the thing that lets you play with the variables)
	
- gazebo --verbose -s libgazebo_ros_init.so -s libgazebo_ros_factory.so
	(call this before spawning your robot)
	
- ros2 run gazebo_ros spawn_entity.py -topic robot_description -entity my_robot
	(after launching gazebo and runing you urdf/xacro files you use this to load them)
	
- ros2 service call /delete_entity gazebo_msgs/srv/DeleteEntity "{name: 'my_robot'}"
	(this deletes your robot)
	
	

------TOPIC---------------------------------------

- ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.5}, angular: {z: 0}}"
	(this makes the ros2_ws/src/car_homework_bringup/launch/car_homework.launch.xml car moves forward)







